<title>JAPAN: Japan Feb soybean imports fall 7.4 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan Feb soybean imports fall 7.4 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's soybean imports in February totalled 405,997 tonnes, down 7.4 percent from the same month a year earlier, Finance Ministry data released on Friday showed.</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Feb 97     Jan 97	Feb 96</p>
<p> Total imports     405,997    471,914     438,328</p>
<p>Major suppliers of soybeans (in tonnes):</p>
<p> U.S.		  369,311    442,383     387,741</p>
<p> China		  14,540     19,133	32,686</p>
<p> Canada		 22,091     10,355	17,884</p>
<p>Total imports in the first two months of calendar 1997 reached 877,911 tonnes against 972,626 tonnes a year earlier.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-7391</p>
</text>
